Snapshot 2026-09-25 (i265): keep-or-drop RD measurement of the three
previously-unmeasured libaom-derived `ZenEnhancement` variants —
`AomIntraEdgeFilter` (ie), `AomRestorationUnitSearch` (ru),
`AomScreenTools` (st). 7092 cells, 0 encode errors, 0 decode errors,
0 dimension mismatches. Evidence for the lead's keep/drop call; no
recommendation beyond the numbers.

host:   i265 — Intel; wall = GNU time %e, cpu = %U+%S around each
        identity_run spawn (overhead identical in every arm), 6 workers
        under run-heavy --mem 8G --jobs 6.
build:  release `identity_run` built from c2f1ffc7eab8 + the new
        SVTAV1_ZEN_RESTORATION_UNIT_SEARCH hook (the hook itself landed
        as c72955d1 on later main). All 7092 cells used this one binary —
        internally consistent. The build predates the concurrent
        refactor/four-variant-removal series on main; the three measured
        arms are independent opt-in flags unaffected by that removal.
data:   benchmarks/aom_keep_or_drop_2026-09-25.csv (7092 rows)
        benchmarks/aom_keep_or_drop_sweep_2026-09-25.py (harness +
        `analyze` mode that produced every number below)
        streams persisted by sha256: ~/tmp/aom-keep-or-drop-2026-09-25/
        (3512 unique .obu, 57 MB)

===================== 1. SWEEP DESIGN =====================

Same cell protocol as aom_features_sweep_2026-09-20.py: `identity_run
crop:<png> 512 512 <qp> <preset>`, aomdec decode, inverse-BT.601 PNG,
fast-ssim2 (`Score:` 0–100) vs the source crop, plus PSNR-Y on the coded
Y planes. qp ∈ {8, 16, 24, 32, 40, 46, 52, 58, 63} — all nine points;
no image or qp was dropped for cost.

Photo class = the 42-image `still_image_tune_v1_subset_2026-09-19.tsv`
subset. **38 of the 42 rows were git-LFS pointers on this host** (only
1000-lilith-photos-general and 8000-lilith-mobile-screenshots are
materialized in imazen-26-png-v3). The objects were fetched through the
GitHub LFS batch API into ~/tmp/aom_kod_images/<oid>.png and sha256-
verified; the harness resolves a pointer row to the cached object, so
the content is byte-identical to what the TSV names. Nothing outside
this workspace and ~/tmp was written.

Screen class = codec-corpus/gb82-sc (local checkout, 10 PNGs;
gmessages at the gates' crop@384,384 content window).

Arms (each vs its own base at the same class/tune/preset/qp):
  photo: p-1 {base, ie, ru, ie+ru ("both"), st};  p6 {base, st}
  screen: p-1 {base, ie, ru, st};  p4 {base, st};  p6 {base, st}
  supplemental: screen p8 {base, st} — see §3 note on why.
  x tune {t1 default, t3 = SVTAV1_TUNE=3}
Env arms: ie=SVTAV1_ZEN_INTRA_EDGE_FILTER=1,
ru=SVTAV1_ZEN_RESTORATION_UNIT_SEARCH=1, st=SVTAV1_SCREEN_TOOLS=1.

BD-rate: per image, log-rate vs quality linear interpolation between qp
points, 40-sample integral over the common quality range (same method as
still_image_tune_v1_analyze_bd.py). win/loss = per-image BD < −0.3% /
> +0.3%. cpuRatio = mean over images of Σ cpu_ms(arm)/Σ cpu_ms(base)
over the 9 qps. err = encode+decode failures (0 everywhere).

