Byte-identity vs base (same class/tune/preset/qp), confirming the zeros:
  ie:   0/378 photo + 0/90 screen cells identical — always active.
  ru:   314-316/378 photo, 88-89/90 screen — mostly inert, small diffs.
  st:   100% identical at p-1/4/6 everywhere; 9/90 at p8 t1; 90/90 at
        p8 t3.

===================== 3. READ =====================

- **AomIntraEdgeFilter**: every cell differs from base; the RD effect is
  a small net loss on photo content — median +0.12% (t1) / +0.51% (t3)
  ssim2 BD, PSNR-Y medians +0.01%/+0.07%, means pulled up by a p75 tail
  of ~+1.1%. 18/42 and 11/42 images improve at t1/t3. On gb82-sc it is
  split (t1 median +0.91% ssim2; t3 median −0.22% ssim2 but +0.52%
  PSNR-Y). Encode +1..+4%. Zero failures.
- **AomRestorationUnitSearch**: RD-neutral. Byte-identical in 83% of
  photo and ~98% of screen cells; median BD 0.000 on both axes in every
  arm, means within ±0.07%. Costs +1.6..+9% encode time for no measured
  gain on this grid.
- **AomScreenTools**: byte-identical in every cell of the *briefed*
  grid — the arm only fills palette/IntraBC when the allintra ladder
  killed BOTH (sc_class5 && palette_level==0 && intrabc_level==0),
  which first happens at preset 8; at p-1/4/6 at least one tool is
  already on, so the arm is structurally inert there. The supplemental
  screen p8 arm measures its active zone: under default tune it saves
  −23.0% mean / −22.3% median ssim2 BD and −28.8% mean / −31.9% median
  PSNR-Y BD, improving 9/10 images, at +31% encode time. Under tune IQ
  at p8 it is again byte-identical — the IQ bundle's
  screen_content_mode=3 already derives tools at min(preset,7), leaving
  no dead-tool state to fill. On photos it cannot act unless the screen
  detector fires.

===================== 4. HONEST LIMITS =====================

- All-intra 512×512 crops only; presets -1/4/6/8 (and photo p6); no
  inter claims. Screen n=10; per-image spreads are small-sample.
- Two quality axes only (ssim2 0-100, PSNR-Y). The st@p8/t1 win is on
  screenshot content where palette/IntraBC are designed to pay; its
  cost on non-screen content at p8+ is unmeasured (detector-gated by
  design, and at p-1/4/6 it is a proven no-op on photos).
- The first sweep run produced 4788 ENC-ERR rows on the 38 LFS-pointer
  inputs (PNG decode InvalidSignature — a harness/data issue, not an
  encoder fault); after materializing the objects those cells encoded
  and decoded clean, and the committed CSV contains only the final
  deduped 7092 rows. Reproducing the photo arm needs
  ~/tmp/aom_kod_images/ (or a materialized imazen-26-png-v3).
- Encode-time ratios are wall/cpu of a spawned-process cell incl.
  ~40-90 ms decode/PNG work per cell excluded — they measure the
  identity_run encode process only.
